Ze-Reviewed-Against: github.com/vishvananda/netlink v1.3.1

The policy writer gives a template with no destination the policy
selector's family. Upstream sets the template family from
nl.GetIPFamily(tmpl.Dst), which answers FAMILY_V4 for any address of four
bytes or fewer, an unset net.IP included. A transport-mode template carries
no addresses, so on an IPv6 policy it goes out as AF_INET, and the kernel's
validate_tmpl (net/xfrm/xfrm_user.c) refuses the policy with "Mode in
template doesn't support a family change". The test is on length rather
than nil, so a non-nil zero-length net.IP is handled too. A template with a
destination keeps the upstream rule.

No upstream pull request is opened yet for this change. Upstream issue 1213
of vishvananda/netlink ("xfrm: three bugs in state read-back, replay window
and template family", opened 2026-08-25) proposes it and has no maintainer
answer yet.

Needs no earlier patch.

Not yet checked against upstream main.

Delete this patch when go.mod requires an upstream release that contains the
change.

diff --git a/vendor/github.com/vishvananda/netlink/xfrm_policy_linux.go b/vendor/github.com/vishvananda/netlink/xfrm_policy_linux.go
--- a/vendor/github.com/vishvananda/netlink/xfrm_policy_linux.go
+++ b/vendor/github.com/vishvananda/netlink/xfrm_policy_linux.go
@@ -170,7 +170,14 @@
 		userTmpl := nl.DeserializeXfrmUserTmpl(tmplData[start : start+nl.SizeofXfrmUserTmpl])
 		userTmpl.XfrmId.Daddr.FromIP(tmpl.Dst)
 		userTmpl.Saddr.FromIP(tmpl.Src)
-		userTmpl.Family = uint16(nl.GetIPFamily(tmpl.Dst))
+		// A template with no destination takes the policy selector's family. The
+		// test is on LENGTH, not on nil: GetIPFamily answers FAMILY_V4 for any
+		// address of four bytes or fewer, so a non-nil zero-length net.IP would
+		// put AF_INET on an IPv6 policy, which is the case this fixes.
+		userTmpl.Family = msg.Sel.Family
+		if len(tmpl.Dst) > 0 {
+			userTmpl.Family = uint16(nl.GetIPFamily(tmpl.Dst))
+		}
 		userTmpl.XfrmId.Proto = uint8(tmpl.Proto)
 		userTmpl.XfrmId.Spi = nl.Swap32(uint32(tmpl.Spi))
 		userTmpl.Mode = uint8(tmpl.Mode)
